---
description: Transaction screens use the purchase invoice shell
alwaysApply: true
---

Transaction entry screens use the purchase invoice shell in `src/components/PurchaseInvoiceManager.tsx`. Do not invent a new page layout.

One status row, then the Document, Notes, and Payment tabs. Header fields and totals stay on the left. The line grid stays on the right. The line editor is the existing line dialog. Footer actions keep the destructive action on the left and Cancel and Save on the right. Do not cover those buttons. Ask Qula is the sparkle button at the right of the title bar. Do not float it over the page or the footer.

Use the classes in `src/components/OpsPage.module.css`: `statusRow`, `headerTabs`, `headerFields`, `invoiceSplit`, `amountBox`, `lineTable`, `lineDialog`, `field`, `quiet`, `primary`, `danger`, `modalActions`. Copy an existing control before adding CSS. Add a class only for a control that does not exist yet.

One message occupies the status row. A problem replaces that message. Do not add a second line above the tabs.

The exchange rate is read-only when the supplier or customer currency is the organisation home currency. A saved master code stays read-only.
